Subject: Generate the engine layout header the unit is compiled against

What this does
  The engine now exposes its object layouts as a struct of sizes and member
  offsets plus a hash, and the generator writes them into a
  `quickjs-aot-layout.h` beside the unit. The unit exports the hash it was built
  with (`qjs_aot_layout`); the engine re-derives the hash from its own structs at
  bind and refuses a unit whose hash differs.

Why we need it
  Generated code reads `JSObject`, `JSShape`, `JSProperty` and `JSString`
  fields at constant offsets, so a change to any of those structs silently
  corrupts an old unit. Until now nothing tied a unit to the layouts it was
  compiled against; `QJS_AOT_ABI` covers the register format and the ownership
  model, not the C structs.

What it adds
  `JSAotGenLayout` and `qjs_aot_layout_hash` in `quickjs-aot-rt.h` (included by
  both the engine and the unit), `js_aot_gen_layout` in the engine, the
  `qjs_aot_layout` unit symbol, the `--layout-header` generator option, the
  generated `quickjs-aot-layout.h`, and the hash check in `aot_unit_present`.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

